{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(n):\n    def sum_proper_divisors(num):\n        # Sum of proper divisors (excluding the number itself)\n        divisor_sum = 1\n        for i in range(2, int(num**0.5) + 1):\n            if num % i == 0:\n                divisor_sum += i\n                if i != num // i:\n                    divisor_sum += num // i\n        return divisor_sum if num > 1 else 0\n    \n    amicable_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        sum_i = sum_proper_divisors(i)\n        if sum_i > i and sum_i <= n and sum_proper_divisors(sum_i) == i:\n            amicable_sum += i + sum_i\n    \n    return amicable_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "\"\"\"\nWrite a python function to find the sum of common divisors of two given numbers.\nassert sum(10,15) == 6\n\"\"\"\ndef sum_common_divisors(a, b):\n    # Find all divisors of both numbers and sum the common ones\n    divisors_a = {i for i in range(1, a + 1) if a % i == 0}\n    divisors_b = {i for i in range(1, b + 1) if b % i == 0}\n    return sum(divisors_a & divisors_b)"}
