{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"Count sequences where each element >= 2 * previous and <= m.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of sequences of length i ending with value j\n    dp = {}\n    \n    # Base case: sequences of length 1\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[(1, j)] = 1\n    \n    # Fill dp table for lengths 2 to n\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):\n            dp[(i, j)] = 0\n            # Previous element must be <= j//2 to satisfy j >= 2*prev\n            for prev in range(1, min(j // 2, m) + 1):\n                if (i - 1, prev) in dp:\n                    dp[(i, j)] += dp[(i - 1, prev)]\n    \n    # Sum all sequences of length n\n    total = 0\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        if (n, j) in dp:\n            total += dp[(n, j)]\n    \n    return total"}
