{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s):\n    \"\"\"Find the length of the longest palindromic subsequence using dynamic programming.\"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n    \n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n    \n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s):\n    # Use dynamic programming to find longest palindromic subsequence\n    n = len(s)\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    # Every single character is a palindrome of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n    \n    # Fill the dp table\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n    \n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
