{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"Find maximum sum of bitonic subsequence - first increasing then decreasing.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n    \n    # Calculate maximum sum increasing subsequence ending at each index\n    inc = [0] * n\n    inc[0] = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                inc[i] = max(inc[i], inc[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Calculate maximum sum decreasing subsequence starting at each index\n    dec = [0] * n\n    dec[n-1] = arr[n-1]\n    for i in range(n-2, -1, -1):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i+1, n):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i]:\n                dec[i] = max(dec[i], dec[j] + arr[i])\n    \n    # Find maximum sum bitonic subsequence\n    max_sum_val = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        max_sum_val = max(max_sum_val, inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i])\n    \n    return max_sum_val"}
