{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence from prefix up to i, including element at k\n    max_sum_up_to_i = 0\n    \n    # Calculate max increasing subsequence sum up to index i\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[idx] = arr[idx]\n        for prev in range(idx):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[idx]:\n                dp[idx] = max(dp[idx], dp[prev] + arr[idx])\n        max_sum_up_to_i = max(max_sum_up_to_i, dp[idx])\n    \n    # Find best subsequence ending at or before i that can connect to k\n    best_sum = 0\n    for idx in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[idx] < arr[k]:\n            best_sum = max(best_sum, dp[idx])\n    \n    return best_sum + arr[k]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr, n, i, k):\n    # Find max sum of increasing subsequence from prefix until i, including element at k\n    if i >= k or k >= n:\n        return 0\n    \n    # dp[j] represents max sum of increasing subsequence ending at index j\n    dp = [0] * n\n    dp[0] = arr[0]\n    \n    # Fill dp array for indices up to i\n    for j in range(1, i + 1):\n        dp[j] = arr[j]\n        for prev in range(j):\n            if arr[prev] < arr[j]:\n                dp[j] = max(dp[j], dp[prev] + arr[j])\n    \n    # Find max sum ending at or before index i that can be extended to include arr[k]\n    max_sum = 0\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[j] < arr[k]:\n            max_sum = max(max_sum, dp[j])\n    \n    return max_sum + arr[k]"}
