{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit and set it\n    temp = n\n    position = 0\n    \n    # Find the leftmost unset bit position\n    while temp > 0:\n        if (temp & 1) == 0:\n            leftmost_unset_pos = position\n        temp >>= 1\n        position += 1\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the next bit\n    if temp == 0 and (n & (n + 1)) == 0:\n        return n | (1 << position)\n    \n    # Set the leftmost unset bit\n    return n | (1 << leftmost_unset_pos)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n):\n    # Find the position of the leftmost unset bit and set it\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # Find the leftmost unset bit position\n    temp = n\n    position = 0\n    \n    # Count total bits in the number\n    bit_count = n.bit_length()\n    \n    # Check each bit from left to right\n    for i in range(bit_count, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n    \n    # If all bits are set, set the bit at position bit_count\n    return n | (1 << bit_count)"}
