{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers up to n using the ludic sieve algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while numbers:\n        # Take the first number as ludic\n        first = numbers.pop(0)\n        ludic.append(first)\n        \n        # If this is the first ludic number (1), continue\n        if first == 1:\n            continue\n            \n        # Remove every k-th number where k is the current ludic number\n        new_numbers = []\n        for i, num in enumerate(numbers):\n            if (i + 1) % first != 0:\n                new_numbers.append(num)\n        numbers = new_numbers\n    \n    return ludic"}
