{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n):\n    \"\"\"Returns all ludic numbers up to n using the sieve method.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n    \n    # Start with all numbers from 1 to n\n    candidates = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic = []\n    \n    while candidates:\n        # Take the first number as ludic\n        next_ludic = candidates[0]\n        ludic.append(next_ludic)\n        \n        # Remove every k-th element where k is the ludic number we just added\n        if next_ludic == 1:\n            candidates = candidates[1:]\n        else:\n            new_candidates = []\n            for i, num in enumerate(candidates[1:], 1):\n                if i % next_ludic != 0:\n                    new_candidates.append(num)\n            candidates = new_candidates\n    \n    return ludic"}
