{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    n = len(matrix)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] stores (max_sum, path_length) for reaching cell (i, j)\n    dp = [[(0, 0) for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    # Initialize the starting cell\n    dp[0][0] = (matrix[0][0], 1)\n    \n    # Fill the DP table\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if i == 0 and j == 0:\n                continue\n            \n            max_sum = float('-inf')\n            path_length = 0\n            \n            # Coming from top\n            if i > 0:\n                sum_from_top = dp[i-1][j][0] + matrix[i][j]\n                length_from_top = dp[i-1][j][1] + 1\n                avg_from_top = sum_from_top / length_from_top\n                \n                if max_sum == float('-inf') or avg_from_top > max_sum / path_length:\n                    max_sum = sum_from_top\n                    path_length = length_from_top\n            \n            # Coming from left\n            if j > 0:\n                sum_from_left = dp[i][j-1][0] + matrix[i][j]\n                length_from_left = dp[i][j-1][1] + 1\n                avg_from_left = sum_from_left / length_from_left\n                \n                if max_sum == float('-inf') or avg_from_left > max_sum / path_length:\n                    max_sum = sum_from_left\n                    path_length = length_from_left\n            \n            dp[i][j] = (max_sum, path_length)\n    \n    return dp[n-1][n-1][0] / dp[n-1][n-1][1]"}
