{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    # dp[i][j] stores (max_sum, path_length) for path ending at (i,j)\n    dp = [[(0, 0) for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n    \n    # Initialize first cell\n    dp[0][0] = (grid[0][0], 1)\n    \n    # Fill first row\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][j] = (dp[0][j-1][0] + grid[0][j], dp[0][j-1][1] + 1)\n    \n    # Fill first column\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        dp[i][0] = (dp[i-1][0][0] + grid[i][0], dp[i-1][0][1] + 1)\n    \n    # Fill rest of the matrix\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(1, n):\n            # Coming from top\n            top_sum, top_len = dp[i-1][j]\n            top_avg = (top_sum + grid[i][j]) / (top_len + 1)\n            \n            # Coming from left\n            left_sum, left_len = dp[i][j-1]\n            left_avg = (left_sum + grid[i][j]) / (left_len + 1)\n            \n            # Choose path with better average\n            if top_avg >= left_avg:\n                dp[i][j] = (top_sum + grid[i][j], top_len + 1)\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = (left_sum + grid[i][j], left_len + 1)\n    \n    final_sum, final_len = dp[n-1][n-1]\n    return final_sum / final_len"}
